    "guidance": "Preferred destination/fixture-anchored choice within the validated distribution. h02 passed 12/12 demonstrated-entry validations; every run ended with the object inside, drawer_position 0.300, and zero IK-unconverged steps, with first exit attainment at steps 198–250. Use when the drawer is open/stable, target_pose is available and rigidly represents the drawer, the block is plausibly held or already over the cavity, and the approach is reachable. It is especially suited by design to alignment, descent, release, retreat, and the fixed handle transition; any benefit under an unseen displaced destination is structural, not rollout-validated. Avoid a missing/jumping target_pose, an attached block far outside demonstrated destination-relative support, a dropped-object recovery state, or infeasible/collision-prone targets. Failure cues are loss of block/TCP following before release, descent outside the cavity, a block still suspended or following after opening, or IK residual/limit warnings. Keep destination anchoring through release and retreat. Transfer to close_drawer only after two causal observations show the block stationary at drawer-floor height and detached; a late handoff can occur with the free gripper at the handle. Use h01 only for a far-displaced but reliably attached transport state, and h03 for local release/retreat ambiguity."
